>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `model_refute`

``` hol4
Refute.model_refute : term -> outcome
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Runs Refute's finite model finder.

`Refute.model_refute tm` is `refute_with [upd_search (Only [ModelFinder])]
tm`: only the `kodkod` backend runs, with every other field of
`!Refute.the_config`, including scopes, solver and encoding options,
output controls, quiet mode, and expectations.

The `kodkod` backend is configured only when the external Kodkodi
component is available; otherwise the result is `Unknown` with a
no-configured-backend reason.  A model's certainty is decided by the
soundness and exactness of its encoding, not by whether a HOL
certificate was built, so a result may be `Genuine` with `cert = NONE`;
`cert = SOME thm` additionally records a certifying theorem.

